# cc_config is its own Bazel module, supplied to converted modules by
# `--override_module` and deliberately never staged into the validation
# tarball. Without this line the root `//...` wildcard walks into it and
# fails to load — `cannot load '//cc_config:config_header.bzl'` — because
# its labels resolve inside that module, not this one. That broke
# `bazel test //...` and `bazel query //...` outright.
#
# Its own tests still run, from its own root:
#   cd cc_config && bazel test //cc_config:all
cc_config
